    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d435">

                <pb facs="0512" n="408" sameAs="frus:frus1932v03/pg408"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">793.94/4321: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to
                        the Consul at Geneva (Gilbert)</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1932-02-20T15:00:00-05:00">February 20, 1932—3
                        p.m.</date></dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>40. Your 86, February 19, 10 p.m. Inform Drummond and Boncour that
                    this Government is in entire sympathy with the endeavor of the Council to have
                    the time limit of the ultimatum extended but that, as hostilities have now begun
                    it would be useless for this Government to take similar action.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                            >Stimson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
